{"name":"Irrigation","hex":"#786c57","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"irrigation","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or process of irrigating, or the state of being irrigated; especially, the operation of causing water to flow over lands, for nourishing plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/irrigation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Irrigation","blocks":[{"text":"Irrigation in agriculture is the practice of applying controlled amounts of water to land to help grow crops, landscape plants, and lawns. Irrigation has been a key aspect of agriculture for over 5,000 years and has been developed by many cultures worldwide. Irrigation helps to grow crops, maintain landscapes, and revegetate disturbed soils in dry areas and during times of below-average rainfall. In addition to these uses, irrigation is also employed to protect crops from frost, suppress weed growth in grain fields, and prevent soil consolidation. It is also used to cool livestock, reduce dust, dispose of sewage, and support mining operations. Drainage, which involves the removal of surface and sub-surface water from a given location, is often studied in conjunction with irrigation. Irrigation and drainage improvements are not necessarily mutually exclusive. Often both may be required together to assure sustained high-level production of crops. For a discussion of the role of drainage practices in agriculture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Fields_SW_from_Sevilla.jpg/330px-Fields_SW_from_Sevilla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irrigation","wikidata":"Q11453"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Bisse.jpg/500px-Bisse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Bisse.jpg/1280px-Bisse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Bisse.jpg/500px-Bisse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traditional irrigation channel in Switzerland, collecting water from the high Alps","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABisse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Pump-enabled_Riverside_Irrigation_in_Comilla%2C_Bangladesh%2C_25_April_2014.jpg/500px-Pump-enabled_Riverside_Irrigation_in_Comilla%2C_Bangladesh%2C_25_April_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Pump-enabled_Riverside_Irrigation_in_Comilla%2C_Bangladesh%2C_25_April_2014.jpg/1280px-Pump-enabled_Riverside_Irrigation_in_Comilla%2C_Bangladesh%2C_25_April_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Pump-enabled_Riverside_Irrigation_in_Comilla%2C_Bangladesh%2C_25_April_2014.jpg/500px-Pump-enabled_Riverside_Irrigation_in_Comilla%2C_Bangladesh%2C_25_April_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Irrigation is underway by pump-enabled extraction directly from the Gumti, seen in the background, in Comilla, Bangladesh.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APump-enabled_Riverside_Irrigation_in_Comilla%2C_Bangladesh%2C_25_April_2014.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Vale_do_S%C3%A3o_Francisco_Pernanbuco.jpg/500px-Vale_do_S%C3%A3o_Francisco_Pernanbuco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Vale_do_S%C3%A3o_Francisco_Pernanbuco.jpg/500px-Vale_do_S%C3%A3o_Francisco_Pernanbuco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grapes in 